    "content": "Troy University is a public, student-centered institution in Alabama, founded over 130 years ago, known as \"Alabama’s International University\". It offers diverse undergraduate, graduate, and online programs, boasting a 93% acceptance rate, a 47% graduation rate, and a 2026 Niche ranking of 25th best online college. Popular majors include Business, Nursing, and Psychology. Key Features and Academic Life Campus Locations: Main campus in Troy, AL, with additional campuses in Dothan, Montgomery, and Phenix City, plus numerous worldwide sites. Academics: Comprised of several colleges, including the Sorrell College of Business and colleges for Arts & Sciences, Education, and Health Sciences. Student Life: 16 Division I athletic teams, over 150 student organizations, and a vibrant, diverse campus culture. Military Friendly: Offers specialized support and programs for active military, veterans, and their families. Admissions and Cost Acceptance Rate: 93%. Admissions Requirements: Typically requires a minimum 2.0 GPA and an ACT score of 20 or SAT score of 950-1030. Net Price: Approximately $12,504 per year. Rankings and Reputation The Princeton Review notes a strong international student presence with students from over 65 countries. Niche ranks it as a top university for online learning and recognizes it as a conservative institution. Median earnings 5 years after graduation are approximately $50,885.",
